{"name":"Rose Turkish Delight","hex":"#db5079","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"rose","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A shrub of the genus Rosa, with red, pink, white or yellow flowers.","A flower of the rose plant."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To make rose-colored; to redden or flush.","To perfume, as with roses."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/rose"},{"term":"delight","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Joy; pleasure.","Something that gives great joy or pleasure."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To give delight to; to affect with great pleasure; to please highly.","To have or take great pleasure."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/delight"}],"entries":[{"title":"Turkish delight","blocks":[{"text":"Turkish delight, lokum or loqum is a family of confections based on a gel of starch and sugar. Premium varieties consist largely of chopped dates, pistachios, hazelnuts or walnuts bound by the gel; traditional varieties are often flavored with rosewater, mastic gum, bergamot orange, or lemon. Other common flavors include cinnamon and mint. The confection is often packaged in small cubes dusted with icing sugar, copra, or powdered cream of tartar to prevent clinging."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/bc/TurkishDelightDisplay.jpg/330px-TurkishDelightDisplay.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Turkish_delight"},{"title":"Rose","blocks":[{"text":"A rose is either a woody perennial flowering plant of the genus Rosa, in the family Rosaceae, or the flower it bears. There are over three hundred species and tens of thousands of cultivars. The plants range in size and form, from trailing and erect shrubs to climbers up to 7 metres (23 ft) in height. Sharp prickles appear on the stems of many species. Their flowers vary in size and shape and are usually large and showy, in colours ranging from white through pinks, reds, oranges and yellows."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e6/Rosa_rubiginosa_1.jpg/330px-Rosa_rubiginosa_1.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Rose"},{"title":"Rose (color)","blocks":[{"text":"Rose is the color halfway between red and magenta, whose hue corresponds to an angle of 330 degrees on the HSV/HSL color wheel."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/2c/Pink-Rose-Sitia-Crete.jpg/330px-Pink-Rose-Sitia-Crete.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Rose_(color)"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/dd/KaymakLokum_%283%29.JPG/500px-KaymakLokum_%283%29.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/dd/KaymakLokum_%283%29.JPG/1280px-KaymakLokum_%283%29.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/dd/KaymakLokum_%283%29.JPG/500px-KaymakLokum_%283%29.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Kaymak lokum, Turkish delight of cream, a specialty of Afyonkarahisar","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AKaymakLokum_(3).JPG"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e5/Sweets_on_Spice_Bazaar_in_Istanbul_07.jpg/500px-Sweets_on_Spice_Bazaar_in_Istanbul_07.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e5/Sweets_on_Spice_Bazaar_in_Istanbul_07.jpg/1280px-Sweets_on_Spice_Bazaar_in_Istanbul_07.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e5/Sweets_on_Spice_Bazaar_in_Istanbul_07.jpg/500px-Swee